{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes","id":588448,"title":"Strix - Synthesis and Banes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-12T13:55:45-07:00","id":588448,"title":"Strix - Synthesis and Banes","content":"Hello, I have a few questions regarding the Strix.<br /> <br /> First of all, I have difficulties with their Synthesis. If it weren't for the Baron, I would have thought the purpose of that power would've been to become a full Kindred and thus, to create a corrupted progeny fully integrated in the vampire society in order to destroy it at some point. Even then, I thought it was a bitter price to pay just for that reward, but hey, the Strix are really mad at the Kindred so why not?<br /> But the Baron just got in the way, since it is said that he, because of his special bond, can sire Kindred...so not the other merged Strix. So, where is the damn point to merge with a host? Strix are much more powerful and free of so many flaws of the Kindred. I fail to see the purpose of that Synthesis.<br /> Moreover, the description of the Baron points out that he can use his Dread powers even as a Kindred, but the Synthesis power says nothing about that. Does a Strix keep his Dread powers when merged?<br /> <br /> Secondly, I am not sure about how to interpret the common banes of the Strix. When a Strix is hit by sunlight, to what extent can it flee from it? For example, if it is struck by a ray, it can flow through a small gap or possess a potential host. As such, it seems that a Strix can avoid the sun in 99,9% of the situations. Also, if the host is burning, the Strix will start suffering and eventually, will die. What prevents the Strix to go out and flee (only in this particular case, if the host is burning and in sunlight I do think that the Strix is truly trapped and cannot go anywhere)? Even when the host is dead, the Strix is cast into the flames, what prevents it to flee at that moment (unless it is done in sunlight once again)?<br /> It is quite disturbing because the rule seems to let some way for the Strix to retreat as it starts to takes damage every minute (which is quite a long time in a fight).<br /> <br /> Can you clarify all this for me, please? :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6912-leamundis","name":"Leamundis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T14:14:49-07:00","id":588475,"title":"","content":"The Baron is something of a special case. Most Stix cannot sire vampires, but the Baron seems to be the exception that proves the rule. As for why they would want to use Synthesis, of course it will vary from one Strix to the next since they all have their own personalities and motivations. But in general, the Strix are actually jealous of the Kindred (that's a big part of why they hate the Kindred so much). They're like Cenobites - explorers of the outer limits of sensation. But they don't have physical bodies, which makes a lot of that exploration quite difficult. As for the common Banes, sunlight and fire are solid to Strix, so if one got caught in a beam of sunlight, it would be like you or me getting stuck inside a wall. Pretty much, they can't get out unless there's a break in the beam. If they're possessing a body that's on fire, they're not going to be able to get out of the body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T00:47:19-07:00","id":588941,"title":"","content":"One of the reasons the Strix really hate Kindred is jealousy over not having a physical form of their own. Synthesis gives a Strix their very own physical form. If there is some magic to remove a Strix from a host, it won't work after Synthesis because the Strix and the host are one being. From a game perspective, it allows Strix to do weird things like embrace normally. Synthesis is a bit vague because it is meant to be used to indicate any strange thing you might imagine, like a Strix-Werewolf or a Strix that <i>can</i> learn Coils or bypass some other limitation that Strix have. If you want a Strix to do something weird that they normally can't then you can use Synthesis to allow it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T00:50:14-07:00","id":588947,"title":"","content":"You simply asumed the Banes of the Strix, by being the same of vampires, should WORK in a similar way.<br /> <br /> They don't. At all.<br /> <br /> It isn't about being hurt by them. It's about treating them as solid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T04:53:42-07:00","id":589031,"title":"","content":"It's a trade-off. Strix are very hard to kill, but they can't operate in sunlight <i>at all</i> without a host. If they're caught out at sunrise with nothing to obstruct them they'll just get slammed over the horizon at 1040 mph without actually taking any damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T09:35:35-07:00","id":589321,"title":"","content":"Thanks for your answers. And about the Dread Powers? Does a Strix keep them if merged or is it also the Baron's specificity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6912-leamundis","name":"Leamundis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T09:42:34-07:00","id":589326,"title":"","content":"Under normal circumstances synthesis turns the strix into a vampire completely, so normally they lose them. The baron seems to have somehow stopped the process halfway. <br /> <br /> Seriously, he's not a good example of the strix rules as written. He's an example of how much you should feel free to bend them if you want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T11:08:05-07:00","id":589372,"title":"","content":"Okay ^^<br /> It was just confusing because some rules lack clarity and this Baron messed it up a little bit more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6912-leamundis","name":"Leamundis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T13:34:30-07:00","id":589499,"title":"","content":"If I recall correctly, when the Strix were originally introduced in Requiem for Rome the Julii clan were created when a Strix merged with the dying Remus. I suspect the Synthesis power was added to the rules to explain that, rather than to explain the Baron. Taking the Baron into account; I'd edit the Synthesis rules in my games such that it produces a Kindred if performed on a living human, a corpse, or a revenant, but it allows the Strix to embrace and use dread powers if performed on a pre-existing Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T16:34:58-07:00","id":589623,"title":"","content":"It's probably easier to just say he has a unique dread power that lets him use it in a weird way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T17:21:00-07:00","id":589663,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think it's something unique to him on account of how long he's possessed that body. I wouldn't render it as a power, so much as a footnote if any other Strix were also capable of doing that.<br /> <br /> Synthesis creates weird shit. Maybe they're like the Mother, and they want to make perfect off-spring. Maybe they're a hellraiser who wants to see what you get when you mix Mage and Strix. Maybe they want to create a &quot;false messiah&quot; for Kindred who think that the person in question is a Spontaneous Embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T02:24:32-07:00","id":590058,"title":"","content":"Still strange to see how this power is basically weakening a lot a Strix, permanently, for the only purpose of messing with the Kindred. Those Owls are really serious when it comes to sacrifice oneself for hatred.<br /> <br /> Another thing, the Kindred disciplines power, does it allow the Strix to use them in Shadow form or only in a host? If it can use them in Shadow form, how are treated Celerity, Resilience and Vigor? And Protean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6912,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6912-leamundis","user":"Leamundis","date":".  question forgotten 07-14-2015, 05:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6912-leamundis","name":"Leamundis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T06:50:33-07:00","id":590177,"title":"","content":"I think it's more accurate to consider the strix using synthesis as <i>becoming</i> the vampire (-like being) they create rather than sacrificing themselves to do it. That's how they view it. They have a weird concept of identity.<br /> <br /> As for disciplines, I <i>think</i> they can use them in shadow form. The six mental ones certainly. Back in first edition they couldn't even learn the physicals or protean, but that's clearly got chucked out the window so I would say that celerity works fine, resilience and vigor work when you're rolling a pool that a material being would use stamina or strength for, respectively, (resilience doesn't seem to add to corpus. I checked the stat blocks) the first dot of protean seems to be something strix can use (since they lost the ability to just phase through walls) but the rest are a bit redundant for a being made of smoke that can flow into any shape it wants anyway.<br /> <br /> Still, they're all very useful in a host, so I can see why a lot of strix would get them anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-14T13:44:46-07:00","id":590458,"title":"","content":"In the end, the best way to understand their powers is as guidelines. Don't bother so much in making sense of every rule about the Strix. They're the ultimately unknowable enemies of the vampires, and each and every rule will find lots of exceptions and unique iterations, so do as they did with the Baron: take the RAW as a general guide and them make YOUR Strix as YOU want it to be.<br /> <br /> Such rules should be more strictly followed only if you where running a game with PC Strix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T06:34:13-07:00","id":593739,"title":"","content":"Given what it says about Cruac, Strix should be able to use their Disciplines as long as it makes sense. Strix don't have blood so they can't spread it around for a power. They would need a host for that. You could hand wave away to some extent, but if the power is partly based on the smell or taste of blood then the Strix would have a problem.<br /> <br /> After a successful Synthesis, the Strix rolls to see if part gets thrown out of the body. Synthesis can be a sort of reproduction method like what Agent Smith can do in the <i>Matrix</i> films. There is a logic to using Synthesis and it can be mostly beneficial to the purpose of a Strix. The logic just isn't human. It won't necessarily make sense to us.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T07:26:34-07:00","id":593763,"title":"","content":"After reading the Synthesis power I came to the conclusion that, as there is no official origin for any of the clans, that the first kindred were Strix that fused with their corpse hosts, gaining clan affinities based off of their personality, and then they discovered the ability to sire progeny (I have a plan for a game where the players are Strix inhabiting corpses who want to have permenant bodies of their own. They eventually reach Shadow Potency 6 and discover synthesis, starting the clans. For the next game I flash forward several thousand years and the Clans in the modern nights have different names, affinities and banes, depending on what the PCs in the last game were like). This requires accepting that the Baron is freaky even for a Strix.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T08:04:13-07:00","id":593795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes?p=593763#post593763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the Synthesis power I came to the conclusion that, as there is no official origin for any of the clans, that the first kindred were Strix that fused with their corpse hosts, gaining clan affinities based off of their personality, and then they discovered the ability to sire progeny (I have a plan for a game where the players are Strix inhabiting corpses who want to have permenant bodies of their own. They eventually reach Shadow Potency 6 and discover synthesis, starting the clans. For the next game I flash forward several thousand years and the Clans in the modern nights have different names, affinities and banes, depending on what the PCs in the last game were like). This requires accepting that the Baron is freaky even for a Strix.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Clans probably all have multiple origins, but this is most likely one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T08:38:16-07:00","id":593861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes?p=593795#post593795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Clans probably all have multiple origins, but this is most likely one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is an idea that I just thought was interesting enough for an entire game. The fact that they would be able to walk around in sunlight but their Childer would not have that luxary is also interesting (I'm assuming that banes wouldn't change after synthesis, and that Dread Powers likely morph into something similar). In a normal game I'd have this as the origin of one Clan, just to heighten the confusion as to 'what is a Kindred?'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T09:26:41-07:00","id":593882,"title":"","content":"I always assumed that the banes <i>would</i> shift. After all, the power itself just says that the corpse &quot;becomes a vampire&quot; with no particular qualifiers excepting them from any aspects of the condition. <br /> <br /> If you think about it, that makes sense. They've merged with their host completely, so now there isn't a fleshy barrier between them and the sun. It's all them. But at the same time physics now has a better hold on them so no poxy little photons are going to stop their big meaty form moving around. A bane isn't going to just sit down and be denied that easily though and so the metaphysical friction causes damage to the vessel. And thus, we have the burning in sunlight thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T11:10:55-07:00","id":594015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes?p=593861#post593861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, this is an idea that I just thought was interesting enough for an entire game. The fact that they would be able to walk around in sunlight but their Childer would not have that luxary is also interesting (I'm assuming that banes wouldn't change after synthesis, and that Dread Powers likely morph into something similar). In a normal game I'd have this as the origin of one Clan, just to heighten the confusion as to 'what is a Kindred?'</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever since the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/560407-ventrue-back-to-nature-bloodline\">Ventrue 'Back to Nature' Bloodline</a> thread, I've been thinking about making a 'Primal' bloodline with Animalism, <i>Dominate</i>, <i>Protean</i>, and Resilience which unties the Ventrue and the Gangrel. The idea is that they are found on all six continents inhabited by humans and typically have names which mean things like 'the first ones&quot; or &quot;the eldest&quot; in the local languages. They would claim to be the original vampires and that both the Gangrel and the Ventrue are just degenerate forms of their bloodline (claims which wouldn't make them popular with either clan). <br /> <br /> I'm probably going to make it so that this is also the default form of a Synthesis produced Kindred. The Gangrel would be the descendents of wild Primals who followed nomadic hunter-gather tribes out of Africa. The Lares (the proto-Ventrue) would have been descended from Primals who used devotions like Reason's Salon and something like the Oath of Abstinence, to turn themselves into the peaceful &quot;household gods&quot; and &quot;ancestral spirits&quot; of Troy.<br /> <br /> Thus, the Ventrue and Gangrel really would be descended from the Strix, and the rest of the clans would be contaminated by two thousand years of mixing blood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T11:51:22-07:00","id":594033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes?p=594015#post594015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ever since the <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/560407-ventrue-back-to-nature-bloodline&amp;quot;]Ventrue</a> 'Back to Nature' Bloodline[/URL] thread, I've been thinking about making a 'Primal' bloodline with Animalism, <i>Dominate</i>, <i>Protean</i>, and Resilience which unties the Ventrue and the Gangrel. The idea is that they are found on all six continents inhabited by humans and typically have names which mean things like 'the first ones&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;the eldest&amp;quot; in the local languages. They would claim to be the original vampires and that both the Gangrel and the Ventrue are just degenerate forms of their bloodline (claims which wouldn't make them popular with either clan). <br /> <br /> I'm probably going to make it so that this is also the default form of a Synthesis produced Kindred. The Gangrel would be the descendents of wild Primals who followed nomadic hunter-gather tribes out of Africa. The Lares (the proto-Ventrue) would have been descended from Primals who used devotions like Reason's Salon and something like the Oath of Abstinence, to turn themselves into the peaceful &amp;quot;household gods&amp;quot; and &amp;quot;ancestral spirits&amp;quot; of Troy.<br /> <br /> Thus, the Ventrue and Gangrel really would be descended from the Strix, and the rest of the clans would be contaminated by two thousand years of mixing blood.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's interesting, although if I wanted a 'primal vampire' strain I'd use a renamed version of Masquerade's Caitiff: you have no affinity disciples, but no clan bane. Your childer will have wildly varying starting disciplines, outlooks, sanity, and even level of kindred-hood, meaning that Clans were developed as being stable.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd put my money on Dracula having no sire being true. If he was an independent ghoul he could have risen as a revenant shortly after his death and then uplifted himself to kindredhoid by diablerie or something like the Coils. He could be clanless, with his childer having a random Clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T12:27:08-07:00","id":594053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes?p=594033#post594033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's interesting, although if I wanted a 'primal vampire' strain I'd use a renamed version of Masquerade's Caitiff: you have no affinity disciples, but no clan bane. Your childer will have wildly varying starting disciplines, outlooks, sanity, and even level of kindred-hood, meaning that Clans were developed as being stable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's pretty much what Revenants are. No Clan Bane, no Affinity Disciplines, weaker blood than normal Kindred... They can't normally sire childer, but there's always the Neglatu Bloodline. And the Neglatu <i>do</i> claim to predate Kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T12:38:33-07:00","id":594057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes?p=594033#post594033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's interesting, although if I wanted a 'primal vampire' strain I'd use a renamed version of Masquerade's Caitiff: you have no affinity disciples, but no clan bane. Your childer will have wildly varying starting disciplines, outlooks, sanity, and even level of kindred-hood, meaning that Clans were developed as being stable.<br /> <br /> Also, I'd put my money on Dracula having no sire being true. If he was an independent ghoul he could have risen as a revenant shortly after his death and then uplifted himself to kindredhoid by diablerie or something like the Coils. He could be clanless, with his childer having a random Clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Caitiff made sense in the context of V:tM, wherein vampires had a single origin (Cain) and branched into the clans. The Clans of V:tR, however, have differing origins, but come together in a case of convergent evolution and cross-pollination via blood sharing. With that dynamic, primitive vampires become more distinct from the other clans not less so. The Hollow Mekhet are a good example of this. With their lack of shadows and wandering reflections they are even stranger than the average vampire. <br /> <br /> My model from a true, &quot;patient 0&quot;, vampire progenitor is either the product of a mystic ritual designed to create a vampiric creature (like the origins of the Mekhet described in their clan book or the Jiangshi) or someone Claimed by a Spirit with vampiric resonances (Blood, Death, Contagion, Predation, etc.) and banes (fire, sunlight, etc.). So, Dracula's life of violence could have attracted spirits of domination, death, and bloodshed, one of which then Claimed him as he was dying (the &quot;Claim&quot; spirit manifestation is a lot like Synthesis). Exposure to true Kindred (and their blood) then imprints some of their resonance onto him, making him more like them with each passing year.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T21:59:31-07:00","id":594418,"title":"","content":"Tough I find the idea of a Claimed-Vampire appealing to some games, I would like to remember that you can't assert that the Clans have distinct origins.<br /> <br /> What every clan have is a barely known history and common legends about its origins. They like to think of themselfs as diferent creatures with shared traits but no common origin, but it isn't a veryfied or veryfiable truth. If he wants to do a single origin, I think he's welcome to do that. It will be true in his game, and one more legend for us to put into ours.<br /> <br /> But I think he didn't tried even that, but simply a common ancestry between Gangrel and Ventrue, not including in the very origin the other clans. They are contaminated, not produced by those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T04:55:35-07:00","id":594639,"title":"","content":"My go-to theory is that the Mekhet were a failed attempt at recreating the Rite of Return from Mummy.<br /> <br /> And I think it would be at least plausible for the Nosferatu to have some connection to Beasts. Nightmares and all that. Maybe they're what happened when a strix used synthesis on one or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:40:41-07:00","id":597101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes?p=594418#post594418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tough I find the idea of a Claimed-Vampire appealing to some games, I would like to remember that you can't assert that the Clans have distinct origins.<br /> <br /> What every clan have is a barely known history and common legends about its origins. They like to think of themselfs as diferent creatures with shared traits but no common origin, but it isn't a veryfied or veryfiable truth. If he wants to do a single origin, I think he's welcome to do that. It will be true in his game, and one more legend for us to put into ours.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, one of the things which makes V:tR more interesting that V:tM (IMO) is the fact that the history and origins of vampires are not clearly defined. So, a Story Teller can define the canon for his own game anyway he wants. That being said, the fact that V:tR clearly departs from V:tM in this way, makes the distinct origins scenario more suitable for V:tR than a common origin scenario. For that matter, the increase in spontaneous embraces as a theme in the game in 2ED, not to mention the inclusion of the Jiang Shi in the core rule book, further re-enforces the plausibility of distinct origins. <br /> <br /> That being said, if one were to go with a single origin scenario, then the Gangrel are the best candidate for &quot;first clan&quot;. Prior to civilization, living among nomadic hunter gatherers, Protean would be vital to survival. All other clans need settled human populations to thrive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T11:52:22-07:00","id":597122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes?p=597101#post597101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True, one of the things which makes V:tR more interesting that V:tM (IMO) is the fact that the history and origins of vampires are not clearly defined. So, a Story Teller can define the canon for his own game anyway he wants. That being said, the fact that V:tR clearly departs from V:tM in this way, makes the distinct origins scenario more suitable for V:tR than a common origin scenario. For that matter, the increase in spontaneous embraces as a theme in the game in 2ED, not to mention the inclusion of the Jiang Shi in the core rule book, further re-enforces the plausibility of distinct origins.<br /> <br /> That being said, if one were to go with a single origin scenario, then the Gangrel are the best candidate for &quot;first clan&quot;. Prior to civilization, living among nomadic hunter gatherers, Protean would be vital to survival. All other clans need settled human populations to thrive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Earth meld would be useful, but not explicitly required. Also 'first clan'? Any 'sole origin' I use is going to have multiple clans come out of it as the 'first' lot, probably the Daeva, Gangrel, Juli, Mekhet, and Nosferatu. No clan is above or below the others, the origin just affected them differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:01:20-07:00","id":597127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes?p=597122#post597122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Earth meld would be useful, but not explicitly required. Also 'first clan'? Any 'sole origin' I use is going to have multiple clans come out of it as the 'first' lot, probably the Daeva, Gangrel, Juli, Mekhet, and Nosferatu. No clan is above or below the others, the origin just affected them differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>So a single event would produce the progenitors of each clan, rather than a single progenitor creating vampires who evolve into separate clans?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T12:05:41-07:00","id":597135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vyrkolash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes?p=597127#post597127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So a single event would produce the progenitors of each clan, rather than a single progenitor creating vampires who evolve into separate clans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, inspired by how every Clan has a 'Snow White' story in the 'Clan Origins' section in the second edition core rulebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T15:54:34-07:00","id":597469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/588448-strix-synthesis-and-banes?p=597135#post597135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, inspired by how every Clan has a 'Snow White' story in the 'Clan Origins' section in the second edition core rulebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neat! Are you going to give them any associations wit the Fae given their fairy-tale origins?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-20T16:32:01-07:00","id":597486,"title":"","content":"Seems a decent enough fit for the Deva origin. <br /> <br /> Which means I have a full set of headcanons now. Yay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}